    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>This flawlessly cut sixty-sided diamond fits in one hand, yet it holds an entire genie empire. High elf magic created it to imprison the infamous genie lords Calim and Memnon, who once ruled and fought over the land now called Calimshan.</p><p>Seen by a creature with Truesight, the beautiful diamond becomes a grotesque sight: more than a hundred genies are trapped inside it, including the physical forms of Calim and Memnon, screaming and straining in agonized fury, their faces pressed against the walls of their crystal prison.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Crystal.</strong> While attuned to the crystal, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Arcane Focus.</strong> You can use the crystal as an @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbagArcaneFocus]{Arcane Focus}.</p><p><strong>Flight.</strong> You have a Fly Speed of 30 feet and can hover.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> You can cast the following spells with the crystal (save DC 18): @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplCreateorDe]{Create or Destroy Water}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplEnlargeRed]{Enlarge/Reduce}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplInvisibili]{Invisibility} (targeting yourself only), and @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMajorImage]{Major Image}.</p><p><strong>Aura of Cold.</strong> The temperature drops sharply in a 20-foot Emanation originating from the crystal. Whenever the Emanation enters a creature’s space, and whenever a creature enters the Emanation or ends its turn there, the creature takes 2d6 Cold damage; a creature takes this damage only once per turn. While attuned to the crystal, you are unaffected by the aura, and you can take a Magic action to turn it off or on.</p><p><strong>Healing/Damage Rays.</strong> While holding the crystal, you can take a Magic action to fire six rays of volatile energy at one or more creatures within 60 feet, aiming them at one target or spreading them among several. For each ray, choose one of the following effects:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Damage Ray.</strong> The target makes a DC 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 6d6 + 6 Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p></li><li><p><strong>Healing Ray.</strong> The target regains 2d6 + 2 Hit Points.</p></li></ul><p>This property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The Artifact has the following random properties (see chapter 7 of the <em>Dungeon Master’s Guide</em>):</p><ul><li><p>1 minor beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li><li><p>1 major detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying the Crystal.</strong> The crystal is destroyed if the creature attuned to it casts the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWish000000]{Wish} spell and wishes for its destruction. Nothing else can harm it. When it is destroyed, all the genies inside are released.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-Dk5xlj5rUTcpbjPK\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ. <em>Fire Rays</em> dépense l’utilisation du jour ; lancez ensuite chacun des six rayons avec <em>Damage Ray</em> ou <em>Healing Ray</em>.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
